# Paper 1 submission source

Target journal: **Data Mining and Knowledge Discovery (DMKD)**.

The submission entry point is `paper1/main.tex`, using Springer Nature's `sn-jnl` class with the `sn-basic` author–year reference style required by DMKD. The active text is assembled from:

- `sections/abstract.tex`
- `sections/introduction.tex`
- `sections/related_work.tex`
- `sections/overview.tex`
- `sections/implementation.tex`
- `sections/experiments.tex`
- `sections/conclusion.tex`

`paper1/latex/acl_latex.tex` is an old ACL-format draft and is not part of the submission build.

## Current evidence

The active title and claims are limited to document-level KG repair. The three
evidence scopes are local structure, document-graph constraints, and support
from the associated source; cross-document alignment and causal inference are
not claimed.

The controlled benchmark in `exps/paper1_repair_benchmark/` contains 1,499
clean/corrupted pairs, 2,998 manifested defects, and a document-group 70/15/15
split. On 225 held-out documents, the Full System obtains 0.9800 defect repair
and 0.9917 triple F1. A new implementation-matched Simple Pipeline obtains
0.9511 and 0.9634; the paired Full-vs-Simple defect test gives `p=0.00235`.

The submission extensions in `exps/paper1_submission_extensions/` add:

- 225 real extraction outputs with no injected defects (77 imperfect graphs,
  302 reference discrepancies);
- full-vs-simple repair on those natural outputs;
- proposal-level constraint-gate auditing;
- actual mixed-stream router execution against heuristic, threshold, random,
  always, and never policies;
- leave-one-domain-out routing;
- a fixed 60-case Claude/Gemma comparison;
- 1K--50K triple profile scaling and incremental updates;
- a frozen 200-item sheet for two independent human annotators.

The Full System reduces natural extraction errors by 0.2775 and reaches 0.9248
triple F1; the Simple Pipeline has -0.5915 error reduction and 0.8807 F1. The
learned router matches the violation and threshold policies exactly, so the
paper treats it as an optional implementation rather than a headline source of
gain. Human agreement remains pending and is not replaced by model judgments.

## Build

```bash
cd paper1
tectonic -X compile main.tex
```

All four figure files cited by the active manuscript are vector PDFs with
embedded **Times New Roman** fonts, including bold text and mathematical
labels. These comprise three method diagrams and one multi-panel experimental
dashboard. The method diagrams follow the author's PNG layouts and visual
motifs, with terminology and control flow aligned to the active manuscript.
Regenerate the figures from the repository root with:

```bash
python3 paper1/make_method_figures.py
python3 paper1/make_submission_figures.py
```

Times New Roman must be installed and discoverable by Matplotlib. The shared style explicitly registers the installed Microsoft core fonts under `/usr/share/fonts/truetype/msttcorefonts/` when available and fails if Times New Roman cannot be found, rather than silently substituting another font. It uses the supported `\varphi` glyph for the router parameter because this font does not contain the alternate mathematical `\phi` glyph.

The author's `figure/method/image1.png`, `image2.png`, and `image3.png` are preserved as original design references. The method script reconstructs text, icons, graphs, and arrows as vector paths and exports matching PDF and editable SVG files; it never overwrites the PNGs. The manuscript includes the PDFs. SVG text also requires Times New Roman on the editing machine. Rebuilding diagrams does not require API requests or model downloads.

To inspect font embedding and confirm that a figure contains no raster images:

```bash
pdffonts paper1/figure/method/image1.pdf
pdfimages -list paper1/figure/method/image1.pdf
```

The manuscript compiles with Tectonic; the template still emits underfull-box and duplicate-destination warnings. These are separate from figure font embedding and vector rendering. The audited author–year bibliography compiles without BibTeX warnings or undefined citations.

The result figures read the archived benchmark, ablation, router, semantic-judge, and failure-audit files directly. Obsolete plots from the former aggregate experiment have been removed so they cannot be mistaken for submission figures.

Experiment details and exact reproduction commands are documented in `exps/PAPER1_EXPERIMENTS_OVERVIEW.md` and `exps/paper1_repair_benchmark/README.md`.

The reference audit, including corrections and source links for all bibliography entries, is in `docs/audits/paper1_reference_check.md` and `docs/audits/paper1_reference_sources.json`.
